# The page is one unversioned file: let browsers and the edge revalidate (cheap 304s via ETag)
# so a deploy shows up at once.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
# Asked for once by a page whose shaders changed (freshShaders in src/main.js), to work around a Chrome
# bug: its WebGPU shader cache keeps an old version's shaders over the new ones, so every visit after an
# update compiled them again. The clear also empties other sites' shader caches in that profile (Chrome
# ignores the origin there). site/fresh-shaders.txt and docs/desktop.md "Shader cache" explain it.
/fresh-shaders.txt
  Clear-Site-Data: "cache"
  Cache-Control: no-store
